Implementation and evidence
- Added an invoked Java `checkForbiddenRetry` case: one configured sync retry produces two CheckForbidden calls, no send-hook calls, and a final `MQClientException` with response code 10003 and the two-attempt message.
- Updated the Java fixture helper to share the same routed Producer setup between retry cases. Fixture SHA-256: `ec20ff084ee066fc71de15e9d744bc091aaced07d1038a8389f12a79d5985b08`.
- Default-route sync send now retries a CheckForbidden hook error only when another attempt remains and the overall send deadline has not expired. The original error is returned when retries are exhausted. Explicit/direct and future paths continue to use their single-attempt/mode-specific flow.
- Added `default_sync_send_retries_check_forbidden_hook_errors_like_java`, which compares the Java fixture, retry count, preserved Rust error, and absence of scripted RPC attempts. Updated Phase 6 audit, Phase 7 Producer matrix, and release checklist.

